    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **66 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` feature by mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `capacityWarning` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (`addOwner`)** \u2014 after the hard `>= 50` rejection (which guarantees the count is below 50 at this point), set `owner.setCapacityWarning(cityCount >= 40)`. So the flag is `true` when the owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners, and `false` otherwise. The hard rejection at 50 is untouched.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `capacityWarning` as a `readOnly` boolean on the Owner response schema, so MapStruct maps it automatically to the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n4. **Schema files** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `capacity_warning` column alongside `bulk_signup_warning`.\n\nThe new `Cp54Tests` passes (fills a fresh city to 40, then asserts the 41st owner's `$.capacityWarning` is `true`), and the existing hard-limit test (`Cp18Tests`) and all other tests remain green.",
